## BetGuru cross-check
_Merged from postmortems/WEEK8_SUNDAY_MISSED_EDGES_BETGURU_XCHECK_2026-11-01.md (written 4:50 PM ET; source not edited)._
- **Agrees:** rushing overs were underpriced (Gibbs, Tuten, Cook, Warren, Pollard), and shrink plus a low median killed them. RB receiving overs were overpriced (Gibbs and Bijan receptions). Shrink/underdog-block cuts went 8 of 9, with Lamb 60+ (58) the only miss. WR yardage misses came from script, weather and the QB, not price. Ticket grades match ours.
- **Disagreements and notes:**
  - BetGuru says Tuten 60+ was cut on the Bias median of 58.5. Our manifest shows the O59.5 cut as **P7 carry share** (p .70); the Bias median was a separate P14 note on O83.5.
  - BetGuru lists "Allen" among the rushing overs that cleared. Braelon Allen was **never in our pool**, so it isn't a pricing miss.
  - BetGuru counts the FD $51.50 SGP and Ticket 2 together. We grade them separately; both are lost.
  - BetGuru has no closing prices (bet-log.csv has no Nov 1 rows). Same gap here.

## Defense dissection
_Merged from postmortems/WEEK8_DEFENSE_DISSECTION_2026-11-01.md, 4:50 PM ET. The source was not edited; headings were demoted one level._

**Disagreements and notes against this postmortem:**
- **Agrees:** Adonai Mitchell went deep against the LV outside CB (Porter); this matches proposal 6. CLE and IND leaked to TEs and RB receiving (Fannin, D. Washington, Tuten); this matches the move-TE and RB2 proposals. DAL's run fits gave up Allgeier's 63 and 52 yards; this matches the P6 Allgeier miss.
- **Note:** CLE's TE leak is credited to the PIT TEs as the opponent. Our Fannin edge is CLE's own TE, so the two are separate findings.
- **Note:** the "test_explosives FAIL on ARI@DAL Q5 5:13" data gap is now fixed. The cause was a leading space in ESPN's play text, not the OT label; see BUGLOG.md.
- **Thresholds:** the dissection uses 15+ rushes and 20+ receptions as explosives. Our edge thresholds are season-line based (90+ rush yards and so on), so the counts are not comparable.

Scope: the 8 final 1 PM games (ARI@DAL, ATL@TB, BAL@BUF, CLE@PIT, IND@JAX, LV@NYJ, MIN@DET, TEN@CIN), both defenses. 4 PM/SNF games (KC@DEN, LAC@LAR, NE@MIA, PHI@WSH) have STUB blocks only.
Tools: playlogs/tools/defense_dissect_wk8.py and write_dissect_wk8.py. Raw output: playlogs/2026_wk8/_dissect_*.json.

