## 4 PM games: KC @ DEN — DEN 28-24 (DEN −1.5, 41.5; over at 52)
- **Edges:** Mahomes 30/41, 321 yards, 3 TD (modeled on the wrong side). Emmett Johnson 5-128 receiving, with TDs of 73 and 38 yards (never in the pool).
- **Game-script read:** This was a **DEN Q4 comeback**: KC led 24-13 going into the fourth and DEN won 28-24. The auto label "favorite close win / shootout" undersells that; it was relabeled in the script file narrative only, and the CSV label was left alone. DEN hit Mahomes 10 times but did not stop the pass, and both defenses gave up their explosives to RB receivers: the KC D's RB-receiving residual was +7.46 and the DEN D's +8.58. Walker had 88% of KC's carries but only 21-69 rushing, so the volume read was right and the efficiency read was wrong.
- **Signal score 2/4:** spread ✅, Walker carry share ✅, total under ❌, DEN pressure suppressing Mahomes ❌.

## 4 PM games: NE @ MIA — NE 24-19 (NE −7, 41.5; over at 43; 75°F, wind 5–9 mph)
- **Edges:** none by the definition. Stevenson 19-82 and Douglas (48-yard TD) came close.
- **Game-script read:** NE ran the favorite run-lean script (Stevenson 19 carries) and sacked Willis 5 times with 9 QB hits, but MIA covered with two late TDs. Cut legs went 8/16 here, the best of the late games, with TE unders (Henry, Raridon) hitting.
